---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base cim="FAQ – Frequently asked questions" leiras="We have collected the most important information about our services, security and backups, as well as questions about contracts and support.">
  <article class="band">
    <div class="wrap-szeles">

      <p class="eyebrow">FAQ</p>
      <h1>Frequently asked questions</h1>
      <p class="lead">We have collected the most important information about our services, security and backups, as well as questions about contracts and support.</p>

      <section class="gyik-szekció">
        <h2>Our services</h2>

        <details>
          <summary>What services does Triox Hosting offer?</summary>
          <div class="valasz">
            <p>We offer three main service models:</p>
            <ul>
              <li><strong>Infrastructure leasing (IaaS)</strong> – leased virtual servers, storage and networking. You decide which software environment runs on it, and we provide the stable, monitored infrastructure behind it.</li>
              <li><strong>Virtual data center (DCaaS)</strong> – a complete, separate environment for a single client: multiple servers, its own network environment, dedicated resources—operated by us.</li>
              <li><strong>Application service (SaaS)</strong> – ready-made applications running in the cloud that you can use on a subscription basis, with no installation or maintenance.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </details>

        <details>
          <summary>Which model should I choose?</summary>
          <div class="valasz">
            <p>In short: if you need a few servers that you manage yourself, infrastructure leasing is the right choice. If you want an entire separate environment with multiple machines and its own network, we recommend the virtual data center. And if you simply want to use a working application without handling the technical background, choose the application service. If you are unsure, we are happy to help you choose the solution that best fits your goals in a short consultation.</p>
          </div>
        </details>

        <details>
          <summary>Which operating system can I run?</summary>
          <div class="valasz">
            <p>We can provide the operating system that fits your needs. We go over the exact options with you in a consultation.</p>
          </div>
        </details>

        <details>
          <summary>Is the service scalable? Can I expand it later?</summary>
          <div class="valasz">
            <p>Yes. The service's resources (compute capacity, memory, storage) can be expanded flexibly as your project grows. There is no need to size for the maximum up front—you can start with a smaller package, and we expand it as you go.</p>
          </div>
        </details>

        <details>
          <summary>Can I request my own dedicated access for my service?</summary>
          <div class="valasz">
            <p>Yes, dedicated access can be provided for the service. We agree on the details based on your needs.</p>
          </div>
        </details>
      </section>

      <section class="gyik-szekció">
        <h2>Security and isolation</h2>

        <details>
          <summary>How is my environment separated from other clients'?</summary>
          <div class="valasz">
            <p>Each client's environment is logically separated from the others. Your data and systems do not mix with other clients' systems; the environments run separately from one another.</p>
          </div>
        </details>

        <details>
          <summary>Are the systems protected from outside access?</summary>
          <div class="valasz">
            <p>Yes. We design our systems so that only the services that are actually needed can be reached from the outside. We restrict access to the narrowest scope necessary.</p>
          </div>
        </details>

        <details>
          <summary>Who can access my data?</summary>
          <div class="valasz">
            <p>Only authorized Triox Hosting staff can access the infrastructure, and only to the extent required for maintenance and operations. Other clients cannot see or access your environment.</p>
          </div>
        </details>

        <details>
          <summary>Where is my data stored?</summary>
          <div class="valasz">
            <p>Your data is stored in Hungary, on infrastructure we operate ourselves. The exact terms are set out in the contract.</p>
          </div>
        </details>

        <details>
          <summary>Is data transfer secure?</summary>
          <div class="valasz">
            <p>Yes. For publicly accessible services, we recommend and support the use of a secure, encrypted connection, and we help you with it during setup.</p>
          </div>
        </details>
      </section>

      <section class="gyik-szekció">
        <h2>Backup and availability</h2>

        <details>
          <summary>Is my data backed up?</summary>
          <div class="valasz">
            <p>Yes. We take regular, automated backups of the environments on a separate backup system, so that a failure does not affect the availability of the backups.</p>
          </div>
        </details>

        <details>
          <summary>How often are backups taken, and how long are they kept?</summary>
          <div class="valasz">
            <p>We adjust backup frequency and retention to your needs. The exact schedule is set out in the service contract.</p>
          </div>
        </details>

        <details>
          <summary>If I delete or break something, can it be restored?</summary>
          <div class="valasz">
            <p>Yes. Both individual data and entire systems can be restored from backups within the retention period. You can submit a restore request through support.</p>
          </div>
        </details>

        <details>
          <summary>What is the guaranteed availability?</summary>
          <div class="valasz">
            <p>Our availability commitment is set out in the service level agreement (SLA), tailored to the service you choose. We announce planned maintenance in advance and aim to carry it out without downtime or during low-traffic periods.</p>
          </div>
        </details>

        <details>
          <summary>What happens if a device fails?</summary>
          <div class="valasz">
            <p>We build your environment so that the service can be restored in the event of a failure. For environments that require higher availability, we design enhanced protection and redundancy.</p>
          </div>
        </details>

        <details>
          <summary>Is there disaster recovery?</summary>
          <div class="valasz">
            <p>For critical systems, we develop a disaster recovery plan. Specific target values are agreed on a case-by-case basis.</p>
          </div>
        </details>
      </section>

      <section class="gyik-szekció">
        <h2>Pricing, contract and support</h2>

        <details>
          <summary>How is the price determined?</summary>
          <div class="valasz">
            <p>Pricing depends on the resources and service level you need, so we prepare a custom quote. There is no “one size fits all” package—you pay only for what you actually need.</p>
          </div>
        </details>

        <details>
          <summary>Is there a long-term commitment?</summary>
          <div class="valasz">
            <p>We set the contract terms together with you. Typically, you can choose between monthly and longer-term arrangements; a longer commitment usually comes with better terms. The details are set out in the quote.</p>
          </div>
        </details>

        <details>
          <summary>How can I order a new service or request a quote?</summary>
          <div class="valasz">
            <p>Please contact us using the contact details on this website. After a short consultation, we assess your needs and prepare a tailored quote.</p>
          </div>
        </details>

        <details>
          <summary>What support do I get?</summary>
          <div class="valasz">
            <p>This is a managed service: we monitor the underlying infrastructure and the backups. You can submit support requests through our help desk. Specific response times and availability windows are set out in the service contract (SLA).</p>
          </div>
        </details>

        <details>
          <summary>Will you help with migration if I move to you from somewhere else?</summary>
          <div class="valasz">
            <p>Yes. We help assess and migrate your existing systems, and we plan the process to keep downtime as short as possible. We agree on the steps with you in advance.</p>
          </div>
        </details>

        <details>
          <summary>Who are Triox Hosting's services for?</summary>
          <div class="valasz">
            <p>Primarily small and mid-sized businesses, software developers, and companies looking for reliable, monitored infrastructure without running their own server room—whether that means serving a single application or a complete, separate environment.</p>
          </div>
        </details>
      </section>

      <p class="nem-talalt">Didn't find the answer to your question? <a href="/en/contact/">Contact us</a>, and we will be happy to help!</p>

    </div>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .wrap-szeles {
    width: 100%;
    max-width: var(--w-max);
    margin-inline: auto;
    padding-inline: var(--pad);
    padding-block: 3rem;
  }

  .lead {
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    color: var(--c-steel);
    max-width: 52rem;
    margin-top: 0.75rem;
  }

  .gyik-szekció {
    margin-top: 3rem;
    padding-top: 2.5rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--c-line);
  }

  .gyik-szekció h2 {
    margin-bottom: 1.25rem;
  }

  details {
    border: 1px solid var(--c-line);
    border-radius: var(--r);
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
    background: var(--c-paper);
  }

  summary {
    font-family: var(--f-display);
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: 0.97rem;
    color: var(--c-ink);
    padding: 1rem 1.1rem;
    cursor: pointer;
    list-style: none;
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 1rem;
    user-select: none;
  }

  summary::-webkit-details-marker { display: none; }

  summary::after {
    content: '';
    width: 0.7rem;
    height: 0.7rem;
    border-right: 2px solid var(--c-brand);
    border-bottom: 2px solid var(--c-brand);
    transform: rotate(45deg);
    flex-shrink: 0;
    transition: transform 0.2s;
    margin-top: -0.25rem;
  }

  details[open] summary::after {
    transform: rotate(-135deg);
    margin-top: 0.2rem;
  }

  details[open] summary {
    color: var(--c-brand);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--c-line);
  }

  .valasz {
    padding: 1rem 1.1rem 1.1rem;
    font-size: 0.94rem;
    color: var(--c-steel);
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .valasz p { margin: 0 0 0.6rem; }
  .valasz p:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }

  .valasz ul {
    padding-left: 1.2rem;
    margin: 0.4rem 0 0;
  }

  .valasz li {
    margin-bottom: 0.4rem;
  }

  .nem-talalt {
    margin-top: 3rem;
    padding-top: 2rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--c-line);
    color: var(--c-steel);
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }
</style>
